"nikolai kingsley" <nikolai@broadway.net.au> writes:

[slow digestion-switching trick]
> i'm sorry. maybe it's because i'm fropped, but this doesn't make much sense.
> can you explain it in another way?

With one or two rings of slow digestion, you don't experience 
normal hunger.  However, if the turn number is of the form 
k*20 + 4 [i.e., 4,24,44,64,..], the game checks whether you 
are wearing a ring on left hand; if so, you get one ordinary 
'hunger'.  Hence, if you remove the ring the turn before 
and slip it back on then, the game won't charge you for 
the ring.  The same game runs with the right hand, the 
difference being that there the turn numbers of the form 
k*20 + 12 [i.e., 12,32,52,..] matter.  

With one ring, you can't play this game, since if you 
slip it off and put it back on, you will be charged for 
one round of ordinary hunger.  Thus, you need two rings 
of slow digestion.  

However, all this is incredibly annoying to do (I 
tried once) and I don't know if somebody ascended 
with this method yet.  The amulet of Yendor, while 
carried, adds hunger every k*20 + 16 turns; you 
would have to drop it then and pick it up again, 
making the method even more annoying.  

